30,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"Wow, I found something really important! It takes so much more time to chase money for individual sessions—six hours a month! That's a lot of evenings gone. I'm worried the next treasurer will be really tired.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The bank statements reveal a concerning lack of reliability in renewals, with many requiring multiple reminders or payment plans. Furthermore, the sign-in sheets show that a significant portion of our membership is entirely inactive.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"My research shows a clear pattern. Many potential members are deterred by the commitment of a full year's fee, and those who do join mid-year require tedious, manual calculations before they feel comfortable signing up.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"Oh boy, the vibe is definitely off! It turns out that adding a door charge for the summer outings really killed the mood for our weekday meetings. People just stopped feeling like they belonged there!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems my suspicions were an understatement. A quarter of the members are doing two-thirds of the attending, and the same nine people are handling all the setup and locking up. We have a small army of ghosts paying for a free ride.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, @Minako, it sounds like we're all seeing things that make the job harder. I also found that most of our costs, like hall hire, have to be paid no matter what. It's a lot of pressure!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, that is exactly the problem. If our fixed costs are constant but our renewal income is unreliable and a large portion of the membership is inactive, we are operating on a very fragile foundation. We cannot afford guesswork.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, while stability is necessary, we must be careful not to create a system that is too rigid. If we make the entry requirements too strict, we risk alienating the very people who keep the club's spirit alive.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minako, I totally agree! It's not just about the money. I found that some of our quieter members feel uneasy about the cost per visit. If they have to weigh it up every time, they just won't come!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, ""feeling the love"" is a luxury we can't afford when nine people are essentially running a concierge service for the rest. If the ""vibe"" is off, it's probably because the regulars are tired of doing all the work.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I don't want anyone to be tired or grumpy. But if we make the treasurer's job too hard by chasing small payments, they'll be tired too! We need a way that's easy for everyone.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, I agree. A system based on frequent, small payments increases the administrative burden and the risk of deficits. We need a structure that ensures predictable income while minimizing the time spent on collections.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, predictability is important, but we must consider the psychological barrier for newcomers. If we insist on large, upfront payments, we will continue to lose potential members who are hesitant to commit to a full year.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, predictability is boring if the room is empty! If we make it too rigid, we're just paying for a hall to sit in by ourselves. We need people to feel like they can just show up without a second thought!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, ""just showing up"" is exactly the problem. We have eighteen people who haven't shown up once, yet they're paying the same as the nine people who actually lock the doors. That's not a club; it's a charity for ghosts.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I feel sad that so many people aren't coming, but I'm really worried about the treasurer. If we pick a system that takes six hours a month just to chase money, it's not very peaceful for them. Let's find a simple way!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, simplicity is a requirement, but it must be paired with financial realism. We cannot ignore that a third of our renewals are delayed. Any system we choose must guarantee the funds are available when the bills are due.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,"It seems we are balancing three different pressures: the treasurer's workload, financial stability, and the accessibility for new members. We must find a solution that doesn't sacrifice our welcoming nature for the sake of administrative ease.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@Minako, exactly! If we treat the club like a business, we'll lose the magic. We need a fee that makes people feel like they're already part of the family, not like they're paying for a ticket to a show!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, ""magic"" doesn't lock the doors or set up the equipment. We're balancing a welcoming atmosphere against the reality of burnout. If we don't reward the regulars, the ""family"" is going to shrink to just those nine people.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
