58,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option A seems the most peaceful for the treasurer! I remember seeing that yearly collection only takes one hour, while chasing small payments takes six. I don't want the next person to lose all their evenings to paperwork.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A provides the most predictable income stream, which is essential given the unreliable renewal patterns I found. It eliminates the risk of mid-year deficits and minimizes the administrative burden on the treasurer.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Option A is efficient, but it creates a high barrier for newcomers. My research showed that many potential members are deterred by a full year's commitment. We risk losing the openness that allows people to drift in.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"@Minako, I'm with you! Option A is just too scary for someone who's not sure yet. But Option B is even worse—it's like a ticket booth! That's exactly what killed the vibe for our weekday meetings.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option A is a fantasy where we pretend everyone is equal. It's the perfect way to keep the ghosts happy while the nine people actually running the place continue to be taken for granted. It's not fair; it's just convenient.,"{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I understand you want it to be fair for the people who work hard, but if the treasurer is too stressed, that's not fair either. Option A is so much easier for them! Does Option C help everyone?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, Option C could potentially address some concerns, but it introduces complexity. If we have multiple tiers, the treasurer must track who is eligible for what, which may increase the administrative burden we are trying to avoid.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, complexity is a risk, but Option C could allow for a lower entry tier. This would lower the barrier for newcomers while still providing a structured way to contribute, potentially preserving the club's welcoming nature.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Minako, now we're talking! Option C sounds like a great compromise. It lets the regulars feel like they're fully invested, but it doesn't make the newcomers feel like they're signing a lifelong contract. It keeps the door open!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, for once, we agree. Option C is the only one that acknowledges the reality of our membership. We can finally stop subsidizing the ghosts and give the regulars a structure that reflects their actual commitment. I'm in.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, if Option C is too hard for the treasurer, maybe we can make the tiers very simple? I really want the person in charge to be happy and not spend all their time on books. Does everyone think Option C is the best?","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, simplicity is key. If the tiers are clearly defined and paid upfront, the administrative burden remains manageable. Given the need for financial stability and the desire to accommodate different levels of activity, Option C is a rational compromise.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,"Option C allows us to maintain a welcoming environment for those who are hesitant to commit, while still ensuring the club's financial needs are met. It balances accessibility with stability without the friction of per-event charging. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Minato, exactly! If we keep it simple, the treasurer stays happy and the members stay excited. No more weighing up the cost every time they want to come out—they just belong! I'm voting for Option C!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, as long as the tiers are set and paid at the start, the treasurer isn't chasing pennies. It's a far more honest system than Option A. I'm voting for Option C.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,"I'm so glad we found a way to make everyone happy! If we keep the tiers simple, the treasurer can have their evenings back and the newcomers will feel welcome. I vote for Option C!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,Option C is the most logical choice. It provides the financial predictability I require while addressing the concerns of the other committee members. It is a sustainable and rational solution for the club. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minako,,"I have already cast my vote for Option C. It is the most balanced approach, ensuring the club remains accessible to newcomers while maintaining the stability we all need. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I'm so happy we're all on the same page! Let's bring back that magic and make sure everyone feels like they truly belong without any second-guessing. I vote for Option C!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Since we've finally stopped pretending that a one-size-fits-all approach works, I'm satisfied. Option C is the only choice that doesn't insult the intelligence of the people actually doing the work. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
